            <div type="translation">
            <p></p></div>

            <div type="commentary">
            <p>cast of right leaf of a consular diptych of Flavius Anastasius (consul 517 CE).  The
                    original, known by the name of Diptychon Leodiense, was preserved for centuries
                    in the cathedral of Saint Lambert in Liège, until it was transferred to Germany
                    in order to be protected during the French Revolution. During the 19th Century,
                    the left leaf was aquired by the Victoria and Albert Museum, while the right one
                    by the Berlin Museum, before it disappeared during World War II.</p></div>
            

